    "Why safety cases must be living documents, not compliance artefacts"
  ],
  "facilitator_notes": "Designed for 4–6 players split across IT security and clinical roles. Facilitator should brief players on their role before starting. IT-track players focus on SIEM, VPN logs, and network isolation. Clinical-track players focus on Bed 4, the drug library, and patient safety decisions. Bed 4 is the main time pressure: if Sarah is not told to plan for hours, Mr Ahmed deteriorates at 8 and 15 minutes and dies at 22. The ICO clock (45 minutes) is the other. Good places to pause for group discussion: Sarah's question about when the monitors come back; David's question on whether CLAIM-HC-001 holds and what the wards lose from isolation; Dr Hartley's isolation and patient-disclosure decisions; Helen's ICO timing (she wants containment first; Article 33 does not); and the Bed 2 pump when it calls the prescribed dose too low."
